{
  "corpus_version": 2,
  "scope": "Draw rules and lifecycle counters over a *sequence* of plies (A64-014.7). A draw is a property of a game rather than of a board, so these cases state an opening position and an ordered list of moves, and assert what the match looks like afterwards. Only the threefold repetition threshold is configured on any variant — the move-limit thresholds are undecided product rules, so no case here can exercise them.",
